<title>INDIA: India's RBI to unwind $1.0 bln forex swaps by Dec.</title>
<headline>India's RBI to unwind $1.0 bln forex swaps by Dec.</headline>
<dateline>JAIPUR, India 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forward dollar swap contracts amounting to $1.0 billion entered into by the Reserve Bank of India will be wound down by December 1996, a senior central bank official said on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;Outstanding swaps of $1.0 billion would be wound down by December 1996,&quot; Usha Thorat, general manager of the RBI, told an annual meeting of the Forex Association of India.</p>
